    a: "Post-operative stress hyperglycemia is common (surgery triggers cortisol, catecholamines, inflammatory cytokines causing glucose intolerance); in diabetic patients, even more pronounced; can impair wound healing, increase infection risk, worsen outcomes; requires insulin therapy (sliding scale or regular monitoring); excessive hyperglycemia (>300) should trigger intervention to bring glucose <180 mg/dL; monitor Q1-2H and adjust insulin",
