    id: "pain-mk-002",
    q: `A 45-year-old female 6 hours post-op from total hysterectomy reports pain 6/10 in her incision. She received morphine 5 mg IV 2 hours ago. She is drowsy but can be aroused. Vital signs: BP 110/68, HR 76, RR 14, O2 sat 95%. She has not had a bowel movement post-op. The nurse offers: Additional opioid now. The patient hesitates: "Won't that make me even more drowsy?" The MOST APPROPRIATE response is:`,
